@HostAddress = http://localhost:5088

### 1. Create Category
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electronics",
  "description": "Smartphones, Accessories and Tech Devices"
}

### 2. Create Brand
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/brands
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Samsung"
}

### 3. Create Unit of Measurement
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/units
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Piece",
  "abbreviation": "Pcs"
}

### 4. Create Main Warehouse
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/warehouses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Main Central Warehouse",
  "code": "WH-MAIN-01",
  "address": "123 Central Industrial Zone, Cairo"
}

### 5. Create Branch Warehouse
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/warehouses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Downtown Branch Warehouse",
  "code": "WH-BRANCH-01",
  "address": "45 Tahrir Square, Cairo"
}

### 6. Get All Warehouses (Dapper Query)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/warehouses?onlyActive=true
Accept: application/json

### 7. Create Product (Catalog)
# Note: Replace categoryId, brandId, unitId with Guids received from steps 1-3 if desired
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra",
  "sku": "SAM-S24U-512GB",
  "price": 45000.00,
  "currency": "EGP",
  "lowStockThreshold": 5
}

### 8. Get Product By Id or Barcode (Dapper Query)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/products
Accept: application/json

### 9. Initial Stock Adjustment (Add 100 units to Main Warehouse)
# Replace productId and warehouseId with actual Guids from above steps
# MovementType 8 = InitialStock, 4 = Adjustment, 1 = Purchase
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/stock/adjust
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "warehouseId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "quantity": 100,
  "movementType": 8,
  "referenceType": "InitialStock",
  "performedBy": "Admin User"
}

### 10. Query Stock Balances (Dapper Query)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/stock/balances
Accept: application/json

### 11. Create Stock Transfer (Transfer 20 units from Main to Branch Warehouse)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/stocktransfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transferNumber": "TRF-2026-001",
  "sourceWarehouseId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "destinationWarehouseId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "createdBy": "Inventory Manager",
  "notes": "Weekly stock replenishment for branch",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "quantity": 20
    }
  ]
}

### 12. Execute Stock Transfer
# Replace transferId with Guid from step 11
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/stocktransfers/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/execute
Content-Type: application/json

"Store Supervisor"

### 13. Query Stock Movement Audit Log (Dapper Query)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/stock/movements?pageSize=20
Accept: application/json

### 14. Create Retail Price List
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/pricelists
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Retail Price List 2026",
  "description": "Standard selling prices for retail customers",
  "isDefault": true
}

### 15. Set Product Price in Retail Price List
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/pricelists/prices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "priceListId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "price": 44500.00,
  "currency": "EGP"
}

### 16. Create Product Batch with Expiry Date (Pharmacy / Expiry tracking)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "warehouseId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "batchNumber": "BATCH-2026-A1",
  "expiryDate": "2026-09-30T00:00:00Z",
  "quantity": 50
}

### 17. Query Expiring Batches (FEFO tracking - Dapper Query)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/inventory/batches/expiring?daysThreshold=60
Accept: application/json
